    <!-- The hold taken on the device itself, through Wireless debugging (SPEC §3.3). -->
    <string name="setup_computer">With a computer</string>
    <string name="selfhold_title">On this device, without a computer</string>
    <string name="selfhold_body">Shinkan can make itself the device owner through Wireless debugging, on a device with no accounts added and connected to Wi-Fi. Then it switches Wireless debugging off, and the hold keeps it off.</string>
    <string name="selfhold_step_developer">1. Turn on Developer options: in Settings, open About phone (or About tablet) and tap Build number seven times.</string>
    <string name="selfhold_open_about">Open About phone</string>
    <string name="selfhold_step_wireless">2. In Developer options turn on Wireless debugging, open it and tap Pair device with pairing code. Settings shows a six-digit code.</string>
    <string name="selfhold_open_developer">Open Developer options</string>
    <string name="selfhold_step_code">3. Keep the code on screen and type it into Shinkan\'s notification: pull the notifications down and reply.</string>
    <string name="selfhold_notify">Show the notification</string>
    <string name="selfhold_step_here">Shinkan is beside Settings: the code can also be typed here.</string>
    <string name="selfhold_notifications_off">Notifications from Shinkan are off, and the code is typed into one. Turn them on in Settings, then tap Show the notification again.</string>
